# SYSPROP's pixel-based lines read dxElt(iElt), which an OPD at that element re-sets to the RAY-GRID
# spacing (DXCALC's slice branch; LOS reads it so) -- at a focus ~0: the lines printed a detector
# pitch of 4.4094850E-12 and lambda/D = 1.2741640E+06 px on the manual's Cassegrain after an OPD
# alone, and the same after INT then OPD (PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (d), measured 2026-10-17 on
# 410aa9d).  Now they print only from a diffraction pitch (dxEltDiffr, set by DXCALC's far-field /
# sphere-to-sphere / Fresnel branches): the hint after the OPD, the INT numbers of EFL_SYSPROP.jou
# after OPD then INT, the hint again after INT then OPD.
# DEADLINE: 120
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
efl
opd 5
/null
sysprop
5
int 5
/null
sysprop
5
opd 5
/null
sysprop
5
# EXPECT: (?s)RMS OPD error.*?pixel-based plate scale needs a diffraction.*?Peak occurs at i=\s+129, j=\s+129.*?lambda/D \(detector px\)\s+=\s+5\.2290937E\+00.*?RMS OPD error.*?pixel-based plate scale needs a diffraction
# EXPECT: Plate scale \(arcsec/px\)\s+=\s+9\.8614033E-03
# EXPECT: Detector pixel pitch \(BaseUnits\)\s+=\s+1\.0744514E-06
# EXPECT-NOT: 4\.4094850E-12
# EXPECT-NOT: 1\.2741640E\+06
# EXPECT-NOT: run OPD, INT
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
